WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.732
Some alerts look scary but are harmless, and some look harmless but are real.

2
00:00:05.732 --> 00:00:10.649
In this demonstration I check three borderline alerts against evidence,

3
00:00:10.649 --> 00:00:17.159
the change calendar and the routine list, before I decide whether each one is a true positive,

4
00:00:17.159 --> 00:00:19.168
a false positive, or routine.

5
00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:23.450
Format-List shows each alert in full.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.234
DB-1, a virus detected on a computer lab PC.

7
00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:35.491
DB-2, impossible travel: a teacher logged in from the campus and five minutes later from Iloilo.

8
00:00:35.491 --> 00:00:41.340
DB-3, a new administrator account on the student information system.

9
00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:44.967
Now the change calendar.

10
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:56.760
CHG-3101 is an approved antivirus test with the EICAR test file, on LAB-PC-15, by jcruz, from one to one thirty.

11
00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:03.710
DB-1 matches all three: same host, same person, inside the window.

12
00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:06.238
It is routine, rule RT5.

13
00:01:06.238 --> 00:01:12.871
And the note says 203.0.113.35 is the school's own VPN gateway.

14
00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:16.262
So DB-2 is not travel at all.

15
00:01:16.262 --> 00:01:23.371
The teacher's second logon came through the school VPN, whose address is placed in Iloilo.

16
00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:28.585
The alert fired, but nothing malicious happened: a false positive.

17
00:01:28.585 --> 00:01:32.139
I record it and ask for the rule to be tuned.

18
00:01:33.239 --> 00:01:38.539
DB-3 has no approved change, and it is not on the routine list.

19
00:01:38.539 --> 00:01:41.903
Let me show the routine list to be sure.

20
00:01:43.003 --> 00:01:44.837
Nothing there explains it.

21
00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:49.351
The account enroll underscore bot only imports enrollment files,

22
00:01:49.351 --> 00:01:55.840
yet it created a new account and made it an administrator on the student information system.

23
00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:02.611
That is a confirmed compromise of an account, a high threat, on a Tier 1 server: P1, ticket now.

24
00:02:03.711 --> 00:02:04.565
Your turn.

25
00:02:04.565 --> 00:02:09.177
In the CTM Virtual Lab, choose Day 6 and Activity 6.2.

26
00:02:09.177 --> 00:02:11.226
Eight borderline alerts.

27
00:02:11.226 --> 00:02:19.937
Check the change calendar, look up every IP address in the asset inventory, and read the routine list.

28
00:02:19.937 --> 00:02:22.328
Only approved changes count.

29
00:02:22.328 --> 00:02:25.743
Watch out for one that is still pending.

